# Copy to mobile/.env for local development.
#
# Where the API lives. A phone cannot reach "localhost" — that address is the
# phone itself, not the machine running the API — so this has to be set to an
# address the device can actually route to:
#
#   Android emulator   http://10.0.2.2:8000     (the emulator's alias for the host)
#   iOS simulator      http://127.0.0.1:8000    (shares the host's loopback)
#   Physical device    http://<your-LAN-IP>:8000
#   Deployed           https://<container-app-hostname>
#
# Expo inlines EXPO_PUBLIC_ variables at bundle time, so a change here needs a
# full reload, not just a refresh. Never put a secret behind this prefix — the
# value ends up in the app bundle in plain text.
EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://10.0.2.2:8000
